{"name":"Mecca Red","hex":"#663f3f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mecca","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of Mecca.\n; a place to which a group of people (for example shoppers) are drawn.","; a place to which a group of people (for example shoppers) are drawn."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mecca"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mecca","blocks":[{"text":"Mecca, officially Makkah al-Mukarramah, is a city in the Hejaz region of western Saudi Arabia and is the capital of Mecca Province. Mecca is considered the birthplace of Islam and the Islamic prophet Muhammad, as well as being the holiest city in Islam."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Great_Mosque_of_Mecca1.jpg/330px-Great_Mosque_of_Mecca1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mecca","wikidata":"Q5806"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/The_Kabah_in_the_Grand_Mosque_of_Makkah%2C_Saudi_Arabia_%2852501405646%29.jpg/500px-The_Kabah_in_the_Grand_Mosque_of_Makkah%2C_Saudi_Arabia_%2852501405646%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/The_Kabah_in_the_Grand_Mosque_of_Makkah%2C_Saudi_Arabia_%2852501405646%29.jpg/1280px-The_Kabah_in_the_Grand_Mosque_of_Makkah%2C_Saudi_Arabia_%2852501405646%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/The_Kabah_in_the_Grand_Mosque_of_Makkah%2C_Saudi_Arabia_%2852501405646%29.jpg/500px-The_Kabah_in_the_Grand_Mosque_of_Makkah%2C_Saudi_Arabia_%2852501405646%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Kabah_in_the_Grand_Mosque_of_Makkah%2C_Saudi_Arabia_(52501405646).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Pilgrims_cover_Arafat%27s_roads%2C_plains_and_mountain_-_Flickr_-_Al_Jazeera_English.jpg/500px-Pilgrims_cover_Arafat%27s_roads%2C_plains_and_mountain_-_Flickr_-_Al_Jazeera_English.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Pilgrims_cover_Arafat%27s_roads%2C_plains_and_mountain_-_Flickr_-_Al_Jazeera_English.jpg/500px-Pilgrims_cover_Arafat%27s_roads%2C_plains_and_mountain_-_Flickr_-_Al_Jazeera_English.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.